#! @Chapter Fusion systems and saturation
#! @ChapterLabel FusionSystemsSaturation

#! In this chapter, fusion systems are given by generators. Let $S$ be a finite $p$-group. A **fusion datum** consists of a subgroup
#! $A_S \leq \textrm{Aut}(S)$ and a list of pairs $(E_i, A_i)$ where $E_i$ is an $S$-centric subgroup of $S$ and $A_i \leq \textrm{Aut}(E_i)$.
#! The fusion system $\mathcal{F}$ of the datum is the smallest fusion system on $S$ containing $A_S$, $\textrm{Inn}(S)$ and $A_1, \dots, A_k$.
#! By the Alperin--Goldschmidt theorem, every saturated fusion system arises in this way, where $E_1, \dots, E_k$ are representatives of the
#! $\mathcal{F}$-conjugacy classes of $\mathcal{F}$-essential subgroups and $A_S = \textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$, $A_i = \textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(E_i)$.
#!
#! The implementation follows the Magma package of Parker and Semeraro <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA"/>. The fusion system is
#! described by its *fusion graph*: the vertices are the $S$-conjugacy classes of $S$-centric subgroups and the edges are the restrictions of the
#! given generators. A connected component is an $\mathcal{F}$-conjugacy class of $\mathcal{F}$-centric subgroups unless it contains a subgroup
#! that is mapped by a generator onto a subgroup which is not $S$-centric. For each $\mathcal{F}$-centric subgroup $Q$ the group
#! $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(Q)$ is computed from a spanning tree of its component (Schreier generators).
#!
#! Saturation is decided by <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Theorem 2.3"/>: $\mathcal{F}$ is saturated if and only if $S$ is fully automized,
#! every $\mathcal{F}$-conjugacy class of $\mathcal{F}$-centric subgroups contains a fully normalized subgroup $P$ with the surjectivity property
#! (for every $P \leq R \leq N_S(P)$ the restriction $N_{\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(R)}(P) \to N_{\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(P)}(\textrm{Aut}_R(P))$ is surjective),
#! and $\mathcal{F}$ is generated by automorphisms of $\mathcal{F}$-centric subgroups.

#! @Section Construction

#! @Description
#! The category of fusion systems given by a fusion datum.
DeclareCategory("IsFusionSystem", IsObject);

#! @Description
#! Constructs the fusion system on the $p$-group $S$ generated by $\textrm{Inn}(S)$, the automorphisms of $S$ in the list `AS` and the
#! groups of automorphisms in the list `L`. Each element of `L` is a group of automorphisms of an $S$-centric subgroup of $S$
#! (its <C>AutomorphismDomain</C>), or a list `[E, gens]` where `gens` is a list of automorphisms of $E$.
#! @Arguments S, AS, L
#! @Returns a fusion system
DeclareOperation("FusionSystemByAutomizers", [IsPGroup, IsList, IsList]);

#! @Description
#! The fusion system $\mathcal{F}_S(G)$ of the finite group $G$ on a Sylow $p$-subgroup $S$. It is given by the automizers of $S$ and of
#! the $G$-centric $G$-radical subgroups of $S$ (up to $S$-conjugacy).
#! @Arguments G, p
#! @Returns a fusion system
DeclareOperation("FusionSystemOfGroup", [IsGroup, IsPosInt]);

#! @Description
#! The $p$-group on which the fusion system is defined.
#! @Arguments F
DeclareAttribute("UnderlyingPGroup", IsFusionSystem);

#! @Section Automizers and centric subgroups

#! @Description
#! Returns true if the subgroup $Q$ of the underlying $p$-group of $\mathcal{F}$ is $\mathcal{F}$-centric.
#! @Arguments F, Q
DeclareOperation("IsCentricInFusionSystem", [IsFusionSystem, IsGroup]);

#! @Description
#! Returns $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(Q)$ as a group of automorphisms of $Q$ for an $\mathcal{F}$-centric subgroup $Q$.
#! @Arguments F, Q
DeclareOperation("AutomizerInFusionSystem", [IsFusionSystem, IsGroup]);

#! @Description
#! Representatives for the $\mathcal{F}$-conjugacy classes of $\mathcal{F}$-centric subgroups.
#! @Arguments F
DeclareAttribute("CentricSubgroupClassRepresentatives", IsFusionSystem);

#! @Section Saturation and invariants

#! @Description
#! Decides whether the fusion system $\mathcal{F}$ is saturated, using <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Theorem 2.3"/>.
#! @Arguments F
DeclareProperty("IsSaturatedFusionSystem", IsFusionSystem);

#! @Description
#! The focal subgroup of a saturated fusion system. It is generated by the elements $x^{-1}\alpha(x)$ with $x \in Q$, $Q$ $\mathcal{F}$-centric and
#! $\alpha \in \textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(Q)$. By <Cite Key="AKO" Where="Corollary I.7.5"/>, $O^p(\mathcal{F}) = \mathcal{F}$ if and only if this is the whole group.
#! @Arguments F
DeclareAttribute("FocalSubgroupOfFusionSystem", IsFusionSystem);

#! @Description
#! The largest normal subgroup $O_p(\mathcal{F})$ of a saturated fusion system: the largest normal subgroup of $S$ contained in every
#! $\mathcal{F}$-centric $\mathcal{F}$-radical subgroup $P$ and invariant under $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(P)$.
#! @Arguments F
DeclareAttribute("PCoreOfFusionSystem", IsFusionSystem);

#! @Description
#! Decides whether two saturated fusion systems on the same $p$-group are isomorphic, i.e. whether there is
#! $\beta \in \textrm{Aut}(S)$ mapping one onto the other. Returns such an automorphism or `fail`.
#! @Arguments F1, F2
DeclareOperation("IsomorphismFusionSystems", [IsFusionSystem, IsFusionSystem]);

#! @Description
#! The number $w(\mathcal{F}, 0)$ of weights of a saturated fusion system with trivial compatible family in the sense of
#! Kessar, Linckelmann, Lynd and Semeraro <Cite Key="KLLS"/>: the sum over the $\mathcal{F}$-classes of $\mathcal{F}$-centric
#! subgroups $Q$ of the number of $p$-blocks of defect zero of $\textrm{Out}_\mathcal{F}(Q)$.
#! @Arguments F
DeclareAttribute("NumberOfWeightsOfFusionSystem", IsFusionSystem);

#! @Description
#! The number $k(\mathcal{F}, 0)$ of <Cite Key="KLLS"/> for the trivial compatible family. It is computed as the sum over the
#! $\mathcal{F}$-classes of pairs $(Q, x)$ with $Q$ $\mathcal{F}$-centric and $x \in Z(Q)$ of the number of $p$-blocks of defect zero of
#! $C_{\textrm{Out}_\mathcal{F}(Q)}(x)$. If $\mathcal{F}$ is the fusion system of a block $B$ with trivial Külshammer--Puig classes and
#! Alperin's weight conjecture holds for $B$ and its Brauer pairs, then this is the number of irreducible characters of $B$.
#! @Arguments F
DeclareAttribute("NumberOfCharactersOfFusionSystem", IsFusionSystem);
